{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates","id":1523495,"title":"The disparate of the Disparates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-03T07:57:47-07:00","id":1523495,"title":"The disparate of the Disparates","content":"Are we ever going to get any info on the Balamob, Mirainohmen, Itz'at, Red Thorn Dedicants, etc.? You know, the handful of Disparate mages hinted at in Mage 20? How about more info on the disparate themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T09:52:21-07:00","id":1523501,"title":"","content":"Well the Balamo\u2019ob have a full write-up in M20 Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T10:51:22-07:00","id":1523643,"title":"","content":"And that's good, but I'd like more info on the Mirainohmen, for example. Also, I'd like to be a bit more up-to-date on the Ahl-I Batini and the Taftani, put some meat on those bones. Maybe make a Tasty Bit on one of those groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T18:38:31-07:00","id":1523673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates#post1523495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we ever going to get any info on the Balamob, Mirainohmen, Itz'at, Red Thorn Dedicants, etc.? You know, the handful of Disparate mages hinted at in Mage 20? How about more info on the disparate themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lore of the Traditions Kickstarter campaign achieved this. It's not currently out yet, but there is going to be a supplement labelled 'Forgotten Ons and Forbidden Orders' that covers some of the non Tradition/Technocracy factions, I believe. So its not out yet, but is in the pipeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T00:25:34-07:00","id":1523682,"title":"","content":"Mmm\u2026 I'm not sure about that I mean, yes; we're getting <b>Forgotten Ones and Forbidden Orders</b>; but I'm not so sure that it will cover anyone outside of the Disparate factions that got write-ups in <b>M20</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T03:20:33-07:00","id":1523691,"title":"","content":"Let's all remember that there were groups mentioned in the very first book that never got any further description. I remember the Fringe Walkers. The Fringe Walkers were described as something between Marauders and sane mages. And nothing has ever been added to that sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T14:32:25-07:00","id":1523738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1523691#post1523691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's all remember that there were groups mentioned in the very first book that never got any further description. I remember the Fringe Walkers. The Fringe Walkers were described as something between Marauders and sane mages. And nothing has ever been added to that sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And nothing will be added to that sentence. Ever.<br /> <br /> I believe you're probably the only person to even remember that obscure single line reference. I doubt any of the editors from the now Onyx Path even know about it.<br /> <br /> And even if they do get informed about this particular subject, I doubt they ever touch that can of worms.<br /> <br /> This, as cool as that might sound, don't expect to read anything about it in the near future. Or in the long future. Or ever.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T20:57:53-07:00","id":1523754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1523738#post1523738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And nothing will be added to that sentence. Ever.<br /> <br /> I believe you're probably the only person to even remember that obscure single line reference. I doubt any of the editors from the now Onyx Path even know about it.<br /> <br /> And even if they do get informed about this particular subject, I doubt they ever touch that can of worms.<br /> <br /> This, as cool as that might sound, don't expect to read anything about it in the near future. Or in the long future. Or ever.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that not every group given a throwaway sentence is developed into something playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T04:12:33-07:00","id":1523764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1523754#post1523754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point was that not every group given a throwaway sentence is developed into something playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T07:50:21-07:00","id":1523999,"title":"","content":"I remember the Fringe Walkers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am quite happy we got the Taftani, and any &quot;Fringe Walkers&quot; we might ever get can be comfortably tucked into the Orphans as a small but dangerous sub-group. <br /> <br /> I half-remembered Forgotten Ones and Forbidden Orders, and it's good to hear that it's still an ongoing project. Thank you for re-informing me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T04:32:24-07:00","id":1524264,"title":"","content":"Mage is a game upon which cultural backgrounds ACTUALLY matter, unlike the other lines (except perhaps for Changeling which could have followed that same path, but I digress).<br /> <br /> Many have criticized VtM for example for having the &quot;beautiful clans&quot;, the 7 original of the Camarilla, being the functional ones, while the rest of the &quot;weirdos&quot; being culture-ethnic related (for example, Tzimisce are Slavic/Eastern Europeans, Assamites are Middle Easterns and so on so forth). The same goes for WtA on a lesser degree.<br /> <br /> For MtA, that actually makes sense, this is a game that relies entirely on cultural identity. Heck, your little &quot;Mage Clan&quot; is not a matter of random cursed blood being injected on you, but rather on what cultural background do you adhere to. If you go to Shangri-la to seek hidden knowledge from monks at the 7 hills, you embrace &quot;Akashianism&quot;, if however you're inducted into a secret cult of satanic Gnosticism you embrace &quot;Hermeticism&quot; and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Disparates, because by the time the writers begun to write about them, it seems they decided to forget culture and just go for what's &quot;exotically cool&quot;. Some Disparates are cool and well though, some are just a joke. Like a group of vietnamese albino mages, or a group of infernalist transsexuals (I believe they are in M20 even?). And there's others equally silly.<br /> <br /> I would like to see for example &quot;samurai/ninja&quot; japanese Disparates, with a strong Shintoist background. Yorubas mages (embracing Caribbean Voodoo and Brazilian Umbanda) and such some.<br /> <br /> But then again, I would want for the Celestial Chorus to be a Christian Tradition and for the Ahl-I-Batin to be an Islamic &quot;Tradition&quot;, rather than they being the &quot;Theosophical Societies of the West and of the East&quot; respectively...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T20:04:54-07:00","id":1536916,"title":"","content":"Wish the Fenian got more love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:39:59-07:00","id":1536967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1524264#post1524264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like the Disparates, because by the time the writers begun to write about them, it seems they decided to forget culture and just go for what's &quot;exotically cool&quot;. Some Disparates are cool and well though, some are just a joke. Like a group of vietnamese albino mages, or a group of infernalist transsexuals (I believe they are in M20 even?). And there's others equally silly.<br /> <br /> I would like to see for example &quot;samurai/ninja&quot; japanese Disparates, with a strong Shintoist background. Yorubas mages (embracing Caribbean Voodoo and Brazilian Umbanda) and such some.<br /> <br /> But then again, I would want for the Celestial Chorus to be a Christian Tradition and for the Ahl-I-Batin to be an Islamic &quot;Tradition&quot;, rather than they being the &quot;Theosophical Societies of the West and of the East&quot; respectively...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that these groups arent a part of the Disparate alliance or, at least, not the main groups (I refer to the circle of Lilith (infernalists) and the vietnamese albinos). The groups that you describe are only a single line in M20 about the groups that could join the Alliance in the near future. This is like go to the Bloodlines section of V20, see the True Brujah and saying that Vampire is about time travels.<br /> <br /> About the characters that you want to create, you can. Nothing stops you from create a Ngoma Yoruba or a Bata'a with Yoruba inheritance. In the second case you could make an orphan / Wu Lung Ninja (but yeah that last option is a bit complex because the Wu lung proud of being chinese and the aislacionism of Japan), even in the secondary groups there is an order of ninjas.<br /> <br /> I agree with you abouth the Alh-i-Batin, more or less. An islamic specific craft is interesting but overlaps with the Taftani and the Celestial chorus in some areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","user":"Metalbird","date":". 06-08-2024, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T08:32:47-07:00","id":1536984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metalbird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1536967#post1536967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that these groups arent a part of the Disparate alliance or, at least, not the main groups (I refer to the circle of Lilith (infernalists) and the vietnamese albinos). The groups that you describe are only a single line in M20 about the groups that could join the Alliance in the near future. This is like go to the Bloodlines section of V20, see the True Brujah and saying that Vampire is about time travels.<br /> <br /> About the characters that you want to create, you can. Nothing stops you from create a Ngoma Yoruba or a Bata'a with Yoruba inheritance. In the second case you could make an orphan / Wu Lung Ninja (but yeah that last option is a bit complex because the Wu lung proud of being chinese and the aislacionism of Japan), even in the secondary groups there is an order of ninjas.<br /> <br /> I agree with you abouth the Alh-i-Batin, more or less. An islamic specific craft is interesting but overlaps with the Taftani and the Celestial chorus in some areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the 2 major &quot;paradigms&quot; of the real world are Christianism and Islam, NOT &quot;da sCience&quot;. And that's pretty much non existent in the game as such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T16:10:29-07:00","id":1537044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1524264#post1524264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is a game upon which cultural backgrounds ACTUALLY matter, unlike the other lines (except perhaps for Changeling which could have followed that same path, but I digress).<br /> <br /> Many have criticized VtM for example for having the &quot;beautiful clans&quot;, the 7 original of the Camarilla, being the functional ones, while the rest of the &quot;weirdos&quot; being culture-ethnic related (for example, Tzimisce are Slavic/Eastern Europeans, Assamites are Middle Easterns and so on so forth). The same goes for WtA on a lesser degree.<br /> <br /> For MtA, that actually makes sense, this is a game that relies entirely on cultural identity. Heck, your little &quot;Mage Clan&quot; is not a matter of random cursed blood being injected on you, but rather on what cultural background do you adhere to. If you go to Shangri-la to seek hidden knowledge from monks at the 7 hills, you embrace &quot;Akashianism&quot;, if however you're inducted into a secret cult of satanic Gnosticism you embrace &quot;Hermeticism&quot; and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Disparates, because by the time the writers begun to write about them, it seems they decided to forget culture and just go for what's &quot;exotically cool&quot;. Some Disparates are cool and well though, some are just a joke. Like a group of vietnamese albino mages, or a group of infernalist transsexuals (I believe they are in M20 even?). And there's others equally silly.<br /> <br /> I would like to see for example &quot;samurai/ninja&quot; japanese Disparates, with a strong Shintoist background. Yorubas mages (embracing Caribbean Voodoo and Brazilian Umbanda) and such some.<br /> <br /> But then again, I would want for the Celestial Chorus to be a Christian Tradition and for the Ahl-I-Batin to be an Islamic &quot;Tradition&quot;, rather than they being the &quot;Theosophical Societies of the West and of the East&quot; respectively...</div> </div> </div> </div>The infernal transsexuals exist in, I believe, exactly one line in M20, where it's mentioned that they're gone now. Basically, Brucato decided that they either can't be salvaged or aren't worth the effort, and wrote them out of the game. I have yet to encounter anyone who was heartbroken over that decision.<br /> <br /> There <i>are </i>some Japanese ninja Disparates in M20, one of the many groups that are potential future recruits for the Disparate Alliance. They have a more full write-up in <b>Dragons of the East</b>. The main problem with them is that as written, they're based more on pop culture ninjas than on authentic Nihon Shinobi; but that can be changed, if <b>Forgotten Ones and Forbidden Orders</b> chooses to tackle them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":"international instead of infernal 06-08-2024, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T08:57:13-07:00","id":1537341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537044#post1537044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The infernal transsexuals exist in, I believe, exactly one line in M20, where it's mentioned that they're gone now. Basically, Brucato decided that they either can't be salvaged or aren't worth the effort, and wrote them out of the game. I have yet to encounter anyone who was heartbroken over that decision.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it would be pretty hard to salvage the Wu Keng. Trans infernalist groomers is an inherently problematic concept even before getting into the fact that there is little to no historical basis in Chinese mysticism for it, or the fact the name Wu Keng loosely translates to &quot;Trap Shaman&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing at this point Brucato is just embarrassed they existed in the first place under his original watch as line editor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T14:33:13-07:00","id":1537359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537341#post1537341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it would be pretty hard to salvage the Wu Keng. Trans infernalist groomers is an inherently problematic concept even before getting into the fact that there is little to no historical basis in Chinese mysticism for it, or the fact the name Wu Keng loosely translates to &quot;Trap Shaman&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing at this point Brucato is just embarrassed they existed in the first place under his original watch as line editor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons want pain and misery for humans individually and as a species. It makes sense that demons would promote and copy destructive behaviors both to make individuals miserable but also to spread bigotries of all sorts to get humans to torture each other. The Wu Keng fit that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> But like the Egyptian Sobek worshippers in the same book, the Wu Keng weren't all that playable. Realistically depicting people either enslaved or ensnared by demons doesn't lead to good RPG play. Such characters are to wounded and restricted to be much fun. They make better mooks than leads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T11:28:15-07:00","id":1537508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1524264#post1524264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many have criticized VtM for example for having the &quot;beautiful clans&quot;, the 7 original of the Camarilla, being the functional ones, while the rest of the &quot;weirdos&quot; being culture-ethnic related (for example, Tzimisce are Slavic/Eastern Europeans, Assamites are Middle Easterns and so on so forth). The same goes for WtA on a lesser degree.<br /> <br /> ..</div> </div> </div> </div>Its probably worth noting the 7 are actually very heavily coded as western, leaning heavily into cultural and social concepts in english speaking countries. It just doesnt egister because of reader bias'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T11:30:27-07:00","id":1537510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537341#post1537341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it would be pretty hard to salvage the Wu Keng. Trans infernalist groomers is an inherently problematic concept even before getting into the fact that there is little to no historical basis in Chinese mysticism for it, or the fact the name Wu Keng loosely translates to &quot;Trap Shaman&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing at this point Brucato is just embarrassed they existed in the first place under his original watch as line editor.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea was that the wu keng are begining to push back against their demonic overlords partly due to trans liberation politics with that subtext weaved into the lore. But it'd be hard to pull off and probably more fuss than worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-16-2024, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T16:09:39-07:00","id":1537529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537510#post1537510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My idea was that the wu keng are begining to push back against their demonic overlords partly due to trans liberation politics with that subtext weaved into the lore. But it'd be hard to pull off and probably more fuss than worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>As close to the Wu Keng as we could get and make it functional would be demons who hunt down potential Mages and trap them into situations of oppression. The desperate mage struggling against those that brutalize them and those they care about are suckered into deals with the demon. But that's a common Nephandi type already. <br /> <br /> Beyond the demon exploiting the victims of human cruelty and greed all else is chrome. It makes little difference in the end whether the trapped Mage was corrupted ahead of the deal or after. And certainly the demons, as they benefit from bigotry of all kinds, would want their pawns to offend sensitivities of as many people as possible. By seeming to confirm bigotries of all types, demons get humans to torture each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T06:26:32-07:00","id":1537610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537508#post1537508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its probably worth noting the 7 are actually very heavily coded as western, leaning heavily into cultural and social concepts in english speaking countries. It just doesnt egister because of reader bias'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point I was making. The original 7, who are the defacto 'functional ones', were cooked in our own familiar western cultural background, while all the others, the &quot;weirdos&quot;, were basically just stereotypes of specific foreign cultures. &quot;Slavs? Dah! They are just a bunch of tyrannical soviets, therefore... Monstrous Tzimisce!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T07:01:42-07:00","id":1537611,"title":"","content":"Anyway, my original point is that Mage begun the right way, but then... It did a bit of &quot;VtM Bloodlines&quot; route (I don't mean the video game, I mean the countless bloodlines that existed previous to whatever game V5 is now). Instead of keeping the cultural context, they just went for the &quot;cool weirdos&quot;. I mean, Dreamspeakers is a nice &quot;catch all term&quot;, and they could leave it there, but they decided that there were the small ones that went their own way... So, while Dreamspeakers may bring together Australian Aboriginals, North American totemists, South American Animists and Siberian Tengri Shamans, maybe even Japanese Shintoists, it's not a stretch of imagination to think that each would also have their own private little clubs of Disparates that didn't went along with the Dreamspeakers program. Sure, Ngoma and Bata'a and whatnot... But, sorry to say, the Umbanda and Candomble from Brazil are NOT the same as those, and neither would they view themselves as such. Well, they don't, actually. Those are, in fact, religions that survived only in Brazil - they don't exist in Africa anymore, at all. At the same time, the South American Natives are predominantly Animistis, as opposed to the North American religions who are Totemic religions. And those are VASTLY different worldviews. <br /> <br /> WoD games were made by Americans and for predominantly American audiences - that's fair enough. I don't have a problem with that. So, I can understand why the Werewolves are based entirely around Totemistic concepts - because I understand that, when Americans think about &quot;Shamanism&quot;, they think about the religions of the natives of their region.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile however, over the rest of the world, most of the &quot;pagan&quot; religions are either Politheistic or Animistic or Fetishist (I won't get in details about that last one right now, but there is a distinction and it's how most African religions work). Shintoism for instance is Animistic, as is the Tengri religion (the religion of the Mongols at the time of the great Khan and also of most of the natives of Siberia).<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is that there are a lot more 'practitioners' of Confucianism, Buddhism, Hinduism, Taoism and Animistic religions than there are groups that worship the ancient Greek Olympians. And yet, you have a group of weirdos that like to cosplay as ancient Furies, just because. The Taftani are another aberration: the ancient pagan religions of the Middle East have all but been eradicated, yet you have a super secret exclusive group to do just that.<br /> <br /> Do you have, by the way, a group of Mages that work within the premisses of Islam? You know, the second largest religion in the world? No, you do not. And while we are at it, what about Christians, you know, just the largest religion in the world. Well, you have a tiny group of medieval zealots that are present in 11 out of every 10 conspiracy theories around, and that's it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you have 3 or 4 groups, depending on how you count, dedicated to different flavors of Gnosticism/Theosophy: Order of Hermes, Choristers, Ahl-I-Batin and Akashics. And not only that, those aren't some fringe weirdos, they are amongst the &quot;big boys&quot; out there.<br /> <br /> So, it is absolutely asinine that the Taftani exist, representing a culture long dead (pre Islamic Arabs), while there isn't a single group of South American tupi-guaranis worshipping their Animistic pantheon on the name of Tup\u00e3, or Tengri mongols worshipping Father Sky.<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, there's even a few new age hippies that decided to worship Wotan (Odin) again. And I have friends here in Brazil that are indeed followers of Wotan. Yeah, insane stuff. I asked them if they prayed for Thor to smash their enemies or if they prayed for Loki to make them cunning, but they were vague and dismissive, so I never again pressed those matters. But hey, they do exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T07:43:29-07:00","id":1537615,"title":"","content":"This comes from assuming that the Traditions are supposed to represent every mystical tradition or religion that's out there. My own way to address the disconnect that you're describing is to instead focus on the Traditions as <i>politics: </i>the reason why certain factions have become Traditions while others are represented by Disparate Crafts is, to a large extent, because those who embraced the Traditions were the ones who agreed with the Council of Magick's \u201cmission statement\u201d. And that mission statement is heavily influenced by Gnosticism. <br /> <br /> The Celestial Chorus is \u201cWestern Theosophy\u201d not because Christianity is Gnostic, but because the unifying tenets of the Traditions favor Western Theosophists over the beliefs of the majority of Christians. Ditto with the Batini, the Order of Hermes, and pretty much every one of the Nine Traditions, if you look at them closely enough. The Disparates, by contrast, are those magical societies that have refused to make any compromises in the name of the Traditions' notion of finding common ground.<br /> <br /> (For the most part, because the Batini, the Children of Knowledge, and the Hollowers were at one point closely associated with the Traditions: the Batini and the Solificati actually were among the magical societies that helped found the Traditions, and the Hollow Ones spent the better part of a century trying to gain membership in the Traditions. And the Bata'a are based on a highly syncretic religion, and would likely jump at the chance to become a Tradition if it was ever offered to them. Which is why I say it's ultimately a matter of politics, not beliefs.)<br /> <br /> I don't view the \u201cTradition vs. Craft\u201d thing to be a matter of superiority, with Traditions being better than Crafts; I chalk <i>that</i> up to the arrogance of the Traditions.The Akashayana are a Tradition; the Wu Lung are a Craft. Don't tell me that the Akashayana are better than the Wu Lung. And that's why I'm not personally opposed to the notion of the Disparate Alliance, so long as it doesn't actually become \u201cTraditions 2.0\u201d. Frankly, I <i>love</i> the idea that you're not required to embrace the notion that \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, ultimately\u201d in order to find common ground with others and forge a viable alliance with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T08:23:41-07:00","id":1537616,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting geo-politics and historical prejudices factor into the formation of the Traditions as well. Shinto usually being associated with the Akashayana over the Dreamspeakers has actual reasoning to it beyond ignorance of what animism is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T09:03:56-07:00","id":1537618,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> , I will say more. The existence of the Disparate makes pretty sense inside the context of the Ascension War, I mean, for one side the Technocracy wants to destroy every craft because their dangerous to the objectives and vision of the former, in the other hand, the Traditions wants the disolution of the Crafts identity and, also, treats them like shit as 2nd citizens or cannon folder. And I don't understand the people who say that this doesn't make sense and after that plays a chronicle with the Traditions, which had a very similar situation before, during the Reinassence. I usually see people who complaints about what have in common a Crusader, a Wu-Lung and a Sister of Hipolite, but this situation happens inside the Traditions too. What have in common an Akashayana, a Celestial Chorister and a Virtual Adept? They only have in common their faction and that's it.<br /> <br /> I think that the main difference from the Traditions is that the crafts distrusts each other. They aren't a stable organization, like the Traditions, which has a long history and common institutions. The Disparate Alliance emerged because the supposed presence of the nephandi in the other two major factions, but this could be only rumors or, at worse, it could result that the Disparate Alliance itself is the result of nephandi influence. And a third point of interest, I think that it could exists frictions inside each craft, between the old guard who wants more freedom from the Alliance , or even in some cases breaking up their relationships with the rests of the Crafts vs the young members who are living in a more and more connected and diverse world, preffering a solid allegiance towards the Alliance as a form to reafirm their identities.The things get even more blurry when you remember that some of the Disparates took a part inside the Traditions during the worst of the Ascension War. How can you know at certain that they are not spies? Or at worst nephandi?<br /> <br /> I think that this drives to a heavy paranoia. When the Technocracy or the Traditions leaves them alone, would the crafts jumps to each other throats? How much you can trust to your friends of other crafts? Can you even trust to your companions of your same craft? How can the Disparate Alliance build common ground apart from their common enemies? How much influence could be from the Nephandi inside the Alliance? The Traditions learnt about the tolerance and the need of live together with each other, but the Alliance hasn't got any of this experience before. And their alternatives are their disappearance or death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","user":"Metalbird","date":". 06-18-2024, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T09:36:18-07:00","id":1537621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523495-the-disparate-of-the-disparates?p=1537611#post1537611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> So, it is absolutely asinine that the Taftani exist, representing a culture long dead (pre Islamic Arabs), while there isn't a single group of South American tupi-guaranis worshipping their Animistic pantheon on the name of Tup\u00e3, or Tengri mongols worshipping Father Sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just noticed this bit and wanted to point out that Zoroastrianism is still very much active in and around Iran, Iraq, and India.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T12:17:38-07:00","id":1537629,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think this is a new observation at all but I do think that part of the observations made above re: the traditions not really serving to accurately reflect what we\u2019d imagine the logical outcome of a world where Awakened Believers can alter Reality would like like, assuming the actual traditions widespread across the globe. <br /> <br /> This has been discussed before but a big reason for this is that Mage was clearly originally written by people involved with/interested in the 90s western (primarily USAmerican) occult revival scene/subculture, with connections to the broader legacy of the western counter-culture in general, with the OG traditions basically reflecting that, plus with some cool ideas for a setting tossed in.<br /> <br /> The Akashyana are both the cool Buddhists &amp; Daoists as well as the carriers of Kung-Fu movie Wuxia vibes (&amp; their og name is a clear reference to Theosophy and the very 90s &amp; very Theosophical infatuation with Tibet). The Celestial Chorus are interesting because they\u2019re caught between antagonistic depictions of the oppressive Church/org. religion institution while also being the focus of some fascination with ideas about alternative-monotheism (see the fascination with Atem &amp; Akenhaten and the idea of a trans-cultural monotheistic conspiracy; maybe also partially inspired by something like Ishmael Reed\u2019s novel \u2018Mumbo Jumbo\u2019) and influence from movement like the Christian-Hippie JesusFreaks. The Cultists of Ecstasy are pretty clearly a mixture of Deadheads, 60s Acid-cases, 90s molly-rockers as well as Discordians &amp; Psychonauts in general. Dreamspeakers are from a fascination with indigenous spirituality in general. Euthanatos are both from a fascination with Hinduism/Dharmic philosophical systems and also just a group of spooky goth assassin Necromancers. The Order of Hermes are classic esotericism: Hermeticism, Alchemy, Freemasonry, Crowleyan Ceremonial Magick, etc. the catch all for a grab-bag of western esoteric concepts. The Society of Ether are pretty unique tho, it was a clever idea to tie in old-school pulp and pseudoscience to the conception of Mage. Verbena are clearly Wiccans, Neopagans, &amp; Witches et all (who were having a big moment in the 90s of course). The og Virtual Adepts are also very clearly relics of the early internet era, inspired by hackers (both irl and in popular conception) and folks like the cyber-utopians and California Ideologists. <br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m sure that for people familiar with Mage, the thesis of the above and most of the examples won\u2019t come as a surprise, but I felt it was worth going to because it captures the contradiction between Mage in its original conceptual formulation and what a reasonable interpretation of its setting principles might otherwise apply (namely: why aren\u2019t the overwhelmingly majority of non-Technocrat Awakened either Christian, Muslim, Buddhist, Hindu, or Animist Will-Workers? How does a relatively small group of western esotericists have such an outsized influence in mage politics?), a contradiction which much of later writing on Mage\u2019s setting was dedicated to papering over, to squaring the circle of.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not certain it\u2019s a circle than can be squared tbh. It may be that one is required to determine what principles one wants to use for the setting of one\u2019s chroniclers and then adjust the setting as needed, however radical those adjustments may be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T13:29:25-07:00","id":1537631,"title":"","content":"In a game about consensual reality, you also have to factor in pop cultural perspectives into the mix. Is hermeticism that prominent in actual modern real world esoteric religious beliefs? No. If magic on the scale described in Mage was a thing would there be plenty of people living out their wizard fascination through it? Definitely.<br /> <br /> Also, there is there the whole fact that it's a game and you have balance authenticity with having a well rounded list of archetypes the players base actually wants to play as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","user":"Becksworth","date":". 06-18-2024, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}